<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eduard Mörike</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1804">1804</a>–<a href="/years/1875">1875</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eduard Mörike was a German poet and Lutheran pastor from Ludwigsburg in Württemberg, associated with the Swabian school of poets. His lyric poems, many set to music by Hugo Wolf, and his novella Mozart on the Way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> (1855) made him one of the finest German writers of the nineteenth century. He also wrote the novel Painter Nolten (1832).</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eduard-morike.jpg" alt="Eduard Mörike" width="300" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eduard_M%C3%B6rike.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
